most appropriate advice?','{"A":"Pulmonary hypertension becomes better during pregnancy.","B":"If she becomes pregnant, termination of pregnancy is not required.","C":"Pregnancy is contraindicated for her.","D":"Maternal mortality in this setting is low.","E":"Sudden death is a rare complication."}','C','Primary pulmonary hypertension is a contraindication to pregnancy and the patient should be advised on the risks of increased maternal mortality in the presence pulmonary hypertension.
