Hypospadias, renal hypoplasia, hydronephrosis, duplication of calyceal system
Brain anomalies
Hydranencephal (1), porencephaly(2), arachnoid cysts, cerebral atrophy, partial agenesis of corpus callosum,
agenesis of septum pellucidum, lissencephaly (3) of medial sides of occipital lobes, Dandy-Walker anomaly
(4)
Eye anomalies
Bilateral congenital cataract, optic nerve hypoplasia, tear duct anomalies, microphthalmia, bilateral iris
defects, corneal opacities
Respiratory tract defects
Tracheomalacia , lung hypoplasia, severe laryngeal hypoplasia, abnormal lobulation of the right lung, right
oligemic (less blood flow) lung
Abdominal wall defects
Omphalocele
Skin abnormalities
Capillary hemangioma, aplasia cutis congenital of the scalp
 
All other medications mentioned carry the risk of congenital malformations at a lower rate compared to valproic acid.
 
(1) Also called hydrancephaly is absence of cerebral hemispheres and replacement of the vacant parts of the cranium with cerebrospinal fluid.
(2) A congenital disorder characterised by presence of cysts or cavities within the cerebral hemisphere.
(3) Literally meaning ‘smooth brain’ is caused by defective central nervous migration during the 12th and 24th weeks of gestation resulting in lack of development of the brain folds (gyri) and grooves(sulci)
(4) Dandy – Walker syndrome is a congenital malformation of the cerebellum with the key feature being complete absence of the cerebellar vermis.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2023','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"131","duplicate_group_id":"exact-aef78c2233e2","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"d17c87d0f5af44888d73","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":960,"source_qid":"131"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
